## P0.8 — Prior art is not yet visible enough

The essay is now careful about internal evidence but still reads as though the architecture emerged mostly from your system + vendors.

Add **one compact related-work disclosure**, not a literature-review section.

Best location:
after the artifact/supply-chain model or before the control-fabric section.

Suggested purpose:

> Similar boundaries are emerging independently. Recent skill-mediated agent architecture work distinguishes stored skills from skill-in-use and connects capability identity, mediation, execution evidence, and feedback. Current BOM work also uses SkillBOM/Skill-BOM for identity, dependencies, and run provenance. I treat that convergence as related work, not as evidence that any one implementation closes the whole chain.

The detailed bibliography can live in an expandable component or sources.

---

## P0.9 — "Agentic Systems Engineering" still reads too much like ownership

Current close:

> "I call the umbrella Agentic Systems Engineering."

Change to:

> "I use Agentic Systems Engineering as the umbrella for this reading path."

or:

> "I place this work within the emerging discipline of Agentic Systems Engineering."

The second is more attribution-safe after the prior-art pass.

