# Scan 3 — Prose and voice

## Strong lines to preserve

These feel like your best voice and should survive structural editing:

> **Copy and paste is fine for discovery, but it will never be a lifecycle.**

> **For five days, "fixed" described one location.**

> **A configured integration is not enforcement; an advisory registration is not a gate.**

> **A skill is small enough to install and large enough to carry intent.**

> **A meeting to approve every local prompt edit would solve a different problem: ensuring nobody uses the system.**

> **The reviewer didn't need a better name or another catalog.**

## Strong idea, tighten wording

Current:

> "The registry was right. My usage was wrong."

Preferred:

> **The registry was right. My deployment was wrong.**

or, more precise:

> **The registry was right. The copy the runtime loaded was wrong.**

Current:

> "Having an agent do something useful once was no longer a challenge."

This is too absolute.

Preferred:

> **Getting useful behavior once was no longer the hard part.**

Current:

> "Those are real questions which demand good answers."

Preferred:

> **Those questions matter. They are not the whole lifecycle.**

Current:

> "Not to even mention if we have multiple worktrees..."

Preferred:

> **Worktrees make it harder: one project can legitimately carry more than one artifact state at once.**

Current:

> "See below two real entries, redacted:"

Preferred:

> **Two redacted entries show the distinction:**

Current:

> "The winning metric will be accepted outcomes with evidence, not activity."

Because the essay explicitly reports no measured outcome improvement, reduce the universal future tense:

> **The metric I care about is accepted outcomes with evidence, not activity.**

or:

> **The useful metric here is accepted outcomes with evidence, not raw activity.**

## Remove

> "To kick this off, let's look at an example of a given skill, which we'll track across the essay."

It is pure stage direction. Start with the incident.

## Small polish

Fix the malformed italic bullet after the YAML block:

`* One tracked copy...*`

It should either be normal prose or a proper italic paragraph with no list marker.

