# Prior art: definitions and contribution claims

**Scope:** this is an editorial/bibliographic review of the supplied research and selected source checks. It is not a patent or trademark opinion. “Earliest found” is not proof of first use. A source's date does not prove what its page said on that date unless the relevant version is preserved.

## Five-term decision table

| Term | What the reports establish | Collision class | Required framing |
|---|---|---|---|
| **agentic artifact supply chain** | R02 found no exact external phrase in its bounded search, but substantial earlier AI-agent supply-chain treatment and very close broad agent-primitive lifecycle work. | Strong conceptual overlap; exact-string negative is inconclusive beyond the search. | Use as an organizing label, not as owned terminology or a new supply-chain idea. |
| **SkillBOM** | Xia's May 29, 2026 near-exact “Skill-BOM”; Liu's June 30 exact spelling; Jia's July 1 SBOM-derived usage. These cover run evidence, component identity and dependencies. | Direct/near-exact lexical and semantic collision. | Define this implementation's fields and semantics, compare them to those meanings, and make no name or base-concept novelty claim. |
| **control fabric** | Older computing/identity usage; BCG's July 2026 federated agent-control framing closely matches the proposed topology. | Longstanding lexical collision plus close architectural collision. | Define the particular interfaces and cross-handoff invariants, not a newly invented federation concept. |
| **deterministic envelope** | Older unrelated timing/safety uses; very close agent/governance uses, including Rao's 2025 essay reported in R04 and 2026 RAILS/other work. | Direct words and close architecture; exact earliest agent use unresolved. | Use descriptively, cite related work and specify implementation/evidence boundaries. Do not claim the learning loop alone is new either. |
| **Agentic Systems Engineering** | Sun et al.'s 2025 academic work; Unstructured in November 2025; OutSystems' March 31, 2026 enterprise framing. | Direct discipline-name and enterprise-meaning collision. | Locate this program within the discipline; show its particular architecture, implementation and experiments. |

Source basis: R02 and R04. Selected checks: V06-V09, V15-V16. Further source recovery is listed in 09.

## A. Agentic artifact supply chain

R02 identifies Cisco's October 23, 2025 agent-supply-chain security framing, July 2026 agent-skill dependency research and JFrog's July 14, 2026 treatment of prompts, skills, instructions, hooks, commands and MCP definitions as governed dependencies. These are not all the same scope, but they remove any credible basis for claiming that the underlying package/supply-chain analogy is new. [R02 §Agentic artifact supply chain]

**Candidate definition:**

> I use agentic artifact supply chain for the managed lifecycle of reusable instructions, context, tools, policies and related assets that shape agent work. It is an organizing label for the architecture discussed here, alongside existing work on agent supply chains and governed agent primitives.

Do not say “the phrase appears available” in public copy. A search's failure to find the exact compound is not a right to claim it, and the essay does not need a lexical priority argument.

## B. SkillBOM

Keep distinct the three existing meanings in R02: component identity/lineage, skill/dependency inventory and run-scoped evidence. A proposed schema that includes all three needs references and an explicit interoperability story. It must not claim run-scoped provenance as the missing innovation when Xia already describes it. [R02 §SkillBOM]

**Candidate definition:**

> SkillBOM already appears in research on skill identity, dependencies and run provenance. Here it names this implementation's manifest; the useful question is which bindings, observations and evidence it preserves, not who owns the term.

**Internal chronology caveat:** the supplied seed `04_SkillMeat_SAM_Spec.md` is self-dated April 26, 2026 and contains a SkillBOM schema. That can support a dated local design record if its history is recovered. It does not establish public priority, a shipped implementation, or a causal relationship to later external publications. Do not erase that independent history by saying the author “adopted it from” a later paper. [L01]

## C. Control fabric

Separate homonyms from relevant overlap. Hardware/control-interconnect usage demonstrates that the words are old, but it is not the important comparison for this essay. BCG's federated governance of multiple agent ecosystems is much closer. The checked July 14, 2026 BCG article also discusses conversion of agentic logic into deterministic code, so neither federation nor that broad graduation direction should be framed as absent from enterprise literature. [R02 §Control fabric; V09]

**Candidate definition:**

> Control fabric is established terminology. I use it for independently operated control systems that preserve compatible identity, authority, policy-decision and evidence records across their handoffs, rather than as another name for one control-plane product.

This defines the author's intended usage without alleging other sources cannot support federation or integration.

## D. Deterministic envelope

R02 and R04 have different search corpora. R02 reports exact AI-agent and hardware/control uses; R04 reports a very close 2025 practitioner article and says it did not find an exact major-vendor/peer-reviewed occurrence in its own retrieved corpus. Neither search-negative statement cancels the other's positive findings. [R02; R04]

R04's reported Rao title includes a ™ symbol. The direct URL and dated original were not recovered by bounded searches in this pass. Preserve the collision as **reported, source recovery required**. The symbol is not evidence here of registration, legal ownership or restrictions.

**Candidate definition:**

> Deterministic envelope is an existing way of describing constraints around probabilistic systems. Here the emphasis is on controls enforced outside model judgment, the evidence that they actually mediate execution, and the lifecycle for promoting or withdrawing reusable automation.

Do not claim “a stricter definition than all prior work.” That comparison has not been established.

**Recommended optional display title:** “What Should Stop Requiring a Model?”

**Subtitle:** “Deterministic envelopes, validated exceptions and the return to automation.”

This is a proposed editorial title, not a rename of E5 or its local slug. It gives the article a distinct question rather than presenting an already-used framework name as a launch.

## E. Agentic Systems Engineering

The current Sun et al. record lists a September 25, 2025 first submission and December 1 revision. Use the versioned title/text before making an exact first-title claim. OutSystems' dated March 31, 2026 announcement is enough to establish close enterprise usage without settling earliest priority. [R02; V15; V16]

**Candidate definition:**

> I use Agentic Systems Engineering as an emerging discipline, not a term I originated. This series examines a particular cross-system architecture for capability, authority, evidence and reuse through the systems I am building and the failures they expose.

Do not manufacture a distinction that OutSystems is categorically closed while this program is open. Its announcement also describes interoperability. Any contrast must identify the concrete boundaries being compared. [V16]

## The most important architectural comparison

The checked Xia reference architecture covers the transition from stored skills to skill-in-use, authority separation, run evidence and feedback into managed supply. This is direct related work for the **architecture**, not simply an earlier occurrence of Skill-BOM. It must be cited when explaining the artifact/use boundary. [V06]

Likewise, R04 presents RAILS as very close to the deterministic/stochastic split and documents precedents for trace-to-workflow or rule compilation. The useful remaining contribution is a specific set of operational contracts and tests; broader integrated novelty remains a hypothesis requiring comparison, not a conclusion of this review. [R04]

## What the author can responsibly emphasize

| Claim | Supported formulation | Evidence needed for more |
|---|---|---|
| Independent development | “These requirements emerged through my implementation work.” | Dated original notes/commits, not retrospective publication metadata alone. |
| Architectural synthesis | “This model connects the following responsibilities in my reference implementation.” | Explicit comparison to related architectures; distinguish implemented from intended. |
| Useful engineering contribution | “This mechanism detected/refused this failure on this path.” | Mechanism revision, actual invocation, decision and test result. |
| Better outcomes | “This treatment improved this measured outcome in this experiment.” | Baseline, task set, repetitions, cost accounting, uncertainty and acceptance criteria. |
| Industry originality | Do not assert on this evidence. | Dedicated exhaustive-enough related-work argument at the specific mechanism level, still bounded. |

## Attribution workflow

Cite overlapping work where the relevant idea appears, not only in a defensive footnote at the bottom. Keep a compact related-work paragraph in E3 and a fuller method/lineage treatment in E5. Store the broader bibliography in the site source notes. Avoid language that falsely attributes the author's historical inspiration to sources discovered only during this review.

## Open items

Earliest dates, the exact Rao source, version-specific term appearances and any new mechanism-novelty claim remain bounded by [07_open_items.md](07_open_items.md).
