## Source-selection priority

Use official versioned documentation for current feature state, original papers for research claims and dated original pages for terminology. Treat a vendor announcement as evidence of what was announced or documented, not independent proof of effectiveness. A practitioner article can establish public wording without becoming authority for empirical claims.

When reports disagree, preserve both statements and decide whether the conflict is about scope, product version, date semantics or genuinely incompatible evidence. Record the decision in the overlay rather than silently replacing the supplied report.

