+<RevisionNote
+  revisedDate=\"September 18, 2026\"
+  note=\"This edition follows external review and a failure in my own deployment process. It sharpens the boundary between approving an artifact and establishing that a particular use was trustworthy.\"
+/>
+
+<ExecutiveSignal
+  whyItMatters=\"Approval attaches to an artifact. Its use happens in a context that approval never saw. A current registry can coexist with stale deployed instructions and unacceptable outcomes.\"
+  takeaway=\"Require separate evidence for declared identity, authorized use, actual execution, and an accepted outcome. Then make deliberate differences visible instead of flattening them.\"
